{"orgCode":"0911","name":"Citizens Redistricting Commission","agencyCode":"0010","agencyName":"Legislative, Judicial, and Executive","description":"The \"Voters First Act\" (Proposition 11) and the \"Voters First Act for Congress\" (Proposition 20) reformed the redistricting process and established an independent 14-member Citizens Redistricting Commission to draw the decennial district boundaries for California's Congressional delegation, state Senate, state Assembly, and Board of Equalization.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":161,"cy":186,"by":186},"positions":{"py":0.9,"cy":0.5,"by":0.5}},"programs":{"id":"exp/0010/0911","kind":"department","name":"Citizens Redistricting Commission","code":"0911","amounts":{"py":161,"cy":186,"by":186},"positions":{"py":0.9,"cy":0.5,"by":0.5},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":161,"cy":186,"by":186}},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0911/0730","kind":"program","name":"Support","code":"0730","amounts":{"py":185,"cy":185,"by":185},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":185,"cy":185,"by":185}},"positions":{"py":0.5,"cy":0.5,"by":0.5},"description":"0730 - SUPPORT\n\nThe Citizens Redistricting Commission drew California's new congressional and state Assembly, Senate, and Board of Equalization districts following the completion of the last decennial census. The districts were drawn based on strict, non-partisan rules delineated in California's Constitution that are designed to ensure fair representation and shall be defended by the Commission as the sole legal defender.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":185,"cy":185,"by":185}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/0010/0911/0730/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":185,"cy":185,"by":185},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":185,"cy":185,"by":185}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"State Operations":{"py":185,"cy":185,"by":185}}}}]},{"id":"exp/0010/0911/0731","kind":"program","name":"Citizens Redistricting Commission","code":"0731"